<!--
    English UI strings.

    ## Why the wording is not literal

    The Chinese original is written for a Chinese reader who already knows what
    a NAS is. A word-for-word translation reads like a manual. So the English
    side is written as if the app were originally English: same information,
    same tone (direct, slightly informal), natural phrasing.

    Examples of deliberate divergence:
    - 「正在寻找 NAS」 -> "Looking for your NAS"  (not "Searching NAS")
    - 「重新扫描」     -> "Scan again"           (not "Rescan" — keeps the verb)
    - 「已切到日间（三端同步）」 -> "Switched to Day (synced to all devices)"
    - 「不配就是空书库」 -> "leave it empty and the shelf stays empty"

    ## Placeholders

    Argument order is identical to the Chinese file. Never reuse a translated
    string across two contexts that need different grammar — add a new key.
-->
